---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import EyeIcon from '../components/EyeIcon.astro';
import RegistryDialog from '../components/RegistryDialog.astro';
import {data, href} from '../lib/data';
const eyes = data('end-eyes', []);
const bosses = data('bosses', []);
---
<Layout title="Bosses & the End" description="Find every End Remastered eye, prepare the required offerings and explore the boss encounters of Towns & Kingdoms.">
 <p class="eyebrow">Handbook / Adventure</p>
 <h1>Bosses & the End</h1>
 <p class="intro">Sixteen eyes connect dungeon expeditions, boss encounters and hidden treasure. Choose twelve different eyes to open the End portal, then plan the encounters and offerings that suit your journey.</p>
 <nav class="toc-inline" aria-label="Boss guide sections"><a href="#end-portal">Opening the portal</a><a href="#eye-routes">Eye routes</a><a href="#eye-guide">Encounter preparation</a><a href="#encounters">All encounters</a></nav>

 <section id="end-portal" class="section prose">
  <p class="eyebrow">End Remastered / The journey</p><h2>Twelve different eyes</h2>
  <ol class="portal-steps">
   <li><strong>Collect twelve distinct eye types.</strong> Each boss in the eye guide drops one matching eye. Several eyes also remain available through treasure, ordinary enemies or crafting, so you can choose your route.</li>
   <li><strong>Locate a Stronghold.</strong> You can still throw ordinary Eyes of Ender to find it. Custom eyes also point the way, with a 10% chance to break when thrown; keep your rare finds for the portal.</li>
   <li><strong>Fill all twelve frames with different custom eyes.</strong> Stronghold frames begin empty. A duplicate eye type is rejected, and an ordinary Eye of Ender cannot fill a frame.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="callout"><strong>Choose your encounters</strong><p>You do not need all sixteen eyes or all sixteen boss kills. A complete set of twelve different types opens the portal. The Wither and exploration dimensions remain accessible without a chapter unlock; individual dimensions and bosses can still have their own entry or summoning requirements.</p></div>
 </section>

 <section id="eye-routes" class="section">
  <p class="eyebrow">Route planner / Sixteen eyes</p><h2>Every eye at a glance</h2>
  <p>The boss route awards the eye directly. The additional routes below remain available alongside it; treasure and ordinary mob routes are chance based.</p>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table class="eye-table"><thead><tr><th>Eye</th><th>Boss route</th><th>Additional routes</th></tr></thead><tbody>{eyes.map((eye:any)=><tr><td><a class="eye-name" href={'#eye-'+eye.id.split(':')[1]}><EyeIcon eye={eye} size={26} />{eye.name}</a></td><td><button class="table-button" data-detail={eye.bossId}>{eye.bossName}</button><div class="table-detail">{eye.dimension}</div></td><td>{eye.alternatives.length ? eye.alternatives.map((route:any)=><span class="route-name">{route.name}</span>) : <span class="subtle">See boss route</span>}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
 </section>

 <section id="eye-guide" class="section">
  <p class="eyebrow">Field guide / Locations & offerings</p><h2>Prepare each expedition</h2>
  <p>Appraise your equipment, allocate your skill points and bring food and recovery supplies before activating an encounter. The level shown is the enemy’s configured floor, not a required player level. Bosses can scale above that floor with nearby players.</p>
  <div class="eye-grid">{eyes.map((eye:any)=><article class="card eye-card" id={'eye-'+eye.id.split(':')[1]}>
   <header class="eye-heading"><EyeIcon eye={eye} size={40} /><div><h3>{eye.name}</h3><code>{eye.id}</code></div></header>
   <div class="tags"><span class="tag">{eye.dimension}</span>{eye.minimumLevel!==null&&<span class="tag tag-gold">Enemy L{eye.minimumLevel}+ · {eye.classification}</span>}</div>
   <h4><button class="table-button" data-detail={eye.bossId}>{eye.bossName}</button></h4>
   <dl class="eye-facts"><div><dt>Find it</dt><dd>{eye.location}</dd></div><div><dt>Begin the encounter</dt><dd>{eye.activation}</dd></div><div><dt>Prepare</dt><dd>{eye.preparation}</dd></div></dl>
   {eye.notableRewards.length>0&&<div class="eye-rewards"><h4>Notable rewards</h4><p>{eye.notableRewards.map((reward:any,index:number)=><>{index>0?' · ':''}{reward.name}</>)}</p></div>}
   {eye.rewardPool.length>0&&<p class="eye-pool"><button class="table-button" data-detail={eye.bossId}>View the equipment reward pool →</button></p>}
   {eye.alternatives.length>0&&<div class="eye-alternatives"><h4>Other ways to obtain this eye</h4><ul>{eye.alternatives.map((route:any)=><li><strong>{route.name}</strong><span>{route.detail}</span></li>)}</ul></div>}
   {eye.notes.map((note:string)=><p class="eye-note">{note}</p>)}
  </article>)}</div>
 </section>

 <section id="encounters" class="section">
  <p class="eyebrow">Reference / {bosses.length} encounters</p><h2>Encounter registry</h2>
  <p>Browse bosses and elite enemies across the pack. Reward pools list possible equipment selections; their entries are alternatives rather than a promise that every item drops together. Appraisal reveals sealed equipment.</p>
  <div class="encounter-notes"><div class="callout"><strong>Enemy levels</strong><p>Ordinary bosses use the higher of their floor or the nearby player’s level +10, up to level 110. Configured elite encounters cap at 100. These values describe enemy scaling, not entry locks.</p></div><div class="callout"><strong>Equipment rewards</strong><p>Dedicated equipment pools require a player kill. A boss’s equipment reward tier is separate from its combat level and weapon handling style. <a href={href('mechanics/#loot')}>Read about appraisal and rarity →</a></p></div></div>
  <div data-registry="bosses"><div class="toolbar"><input type="search" data-filter="query" placeholder="Search an encounter or mod…" aria-label="Search bosses"/><select data-filter="modName" aria-label="Filter by mod"><option value="">All mods</option></select><select data-filter="classification" aria-label="Filter encounter type"><option value="">All encounters</option></select></div><div class="results-meta"><span data-count>Finding encounters…</span><span>Select an encounter for its rewards</span></div><div class="weapon-grid" data-results></div><div class="pagination"><button data-prev disabled>← Previous</button><span data-page-label>1 / 1</span><button data-next>Next →</button></div></div>
 </section>
 <RegistryDialog />
 <script>import '../scripts/registry';</script>
</Layout>
<style>
 .portal-steps{padding-left:24px}.portal-steps li{padding-left:5px;margin:15px 0;line-height:1.8}
 .eye-table td{vertical-align:top}.eye-name{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap}.route-name{display:block;font-size:14px;line-height:1.8}
 .eye-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:18px;margin-top:26px}.eye-card{padding:26px;scroll-margin-top:95px}.eye-heading{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;margin-bottom:18px}.eye-heading h3{margin:0 0 5px;font-size:21px}.eye-heading>div{min-width:0}.eye-heading code{overflow-wrap:anywhere;font-size:13px;color:var(--muted)}.eye-card>.tags{margin-bottom:22px}.eye-card h4{font-size:14px;margin:20px 0 9px}.eye-card h4>.table-button{font-size:15px;font-weight:650;text-align:left}.eye-facts{margin:0}.eye-facts>div{margin-top:15px}.eye-facts dt{font-size:13px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.11em;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:5px}.eye-facts dd{margin:0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--muted)}.eye-rewards p{font-size:16px;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:0}.eye-pool{margin:8px 0 0!important}.eye-pool button{font-size:14px}.eye-alternatives{border-top:1px solid var(--border);margin-top:24px;padding-top:4px}.eye-alternatives ul{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0}.eye-alternatives li{margin:12px 0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.8}.eye-alternatives li strong,.eye-alternatives li span{display:block}.eye-alternatives li span{color:var(--muted)}.eye-card .eye-note{font-size:14px;padding-left:12px;border-left:2px solid var(--border);margin-top:17px!important}.encounter-notes{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:18px;margin:24px 0}.encounter-notes .callout{margin:0}.encounter-notes p{font-size:16px;margin-bottom:0}
 @media(max-width:760px){.eye-grid,.encounter-notes{grid-template-columns:1fr}.eye-card{padding:22px}.eye-table th,.eye-table td{padding:14px 12px}.eye-name{white-space:normal}}
</style>
